WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.354
Lab 2 runs the same path in your
own test tenant, worldwide or G C C,

2
00:00:04.354 --> 00:00:10.066
never production, with a Workload Identities
Premium trial or license, one test app

3
00:00:10.066 --> 00:00:15.612
registration with a certificate, and a
host whose public egress address you know.

4
00:00:15.612 --> 00:00:19.334
Write a scope with the test
app's enterprise application

5
00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.263
object I D in Ring 1, and
plan with a reading app.

6
00:00:22.263 --> 00:00:27.725
Apply report-only, and generate sign-ins
from inside and outside the egress range.

7
00:00:27.725 --> 00:00:32.458
Then, in a separate change, after at
least fourteen days with the ring clear,

8
00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:36.725
enforce Ring 1, and watch a token
from outside the range get blocked.

9
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:40.590
To back it out, step seven removes
Ring 1 from the enforcement

10
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.300
record and applies, so both
policies return to report-only.

11
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.950
Then you turn them off or delete them by
hand, because the code never deletes.

12
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.170
The authors haven't run Lab 2.
